 631	 * the LCPU off, re-init the mailbox, re-register the RX callback
 632	 * (controller_init clears the adapter env) and boot a fresh LCPU
 633	 * (patch install + RF calibration + ring sync).  After this the
 634	 * controller answers HCI again and the zblue host can tear itself
 635	 * down cleanly.  Must run from a context where blocking is OK.
